# Angelina Hybrid Cloud — Caddyfile for the Cloud_Instance (Task 12.4)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# STAGED ARTIFACT — not installed on any VM. Install to /etc/caddy/Caddyfile
# on the cloud VM (see install-caddy.sh / README.md).
#
# Caddy terminates HTTPS (automatic Let's Encrypt for the DuckDNS name) and
# reverse-proxies to Angelina bound on loopback 127.0.0.1:8080. Angelina's
# 8080 is never exposed publicly; only 80 (ACME challenge) and 443 (HTTPS)
# are opened at the firewall (Req 8.1, 8.4, 8.7).
#
# ACME EMAIL — REQUIRED, DO NOT hardcode a real address here.
# Caddy needs an ACME contact email for Let's Encrypt. Supply it as the
# CADDY_EMAIL environment variable (e.g. in /etc/caddy/caddy.env referenced by
# the caddy systemd unit, or exported before `caddy run`). The global option
# below reads {$CADDY_EMAIL}. If you prefer, replace {$CADDY_EMAIL} with the
# operator's real address directly — but keep it OUT of version control.

{
	email {$CADDY_EMAIL}
}

YOUR_SUBDOMAIN.duckdns.org {
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8080
}
